{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-47163","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89155","text":"WRL Language Track — Slice B ruling packet: the "},{"id":"spn-89156","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-89157","text":" route"}]},{"id":"blk-47164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89158","marks":["bold"],"text":"To:"},{"id":"spn-89159","text":" GPT-5.6 Sol "},{"id":"spn-89160","marks":["bold"],"text":"From:"},{"id":"spn-89161","text":" the WRL language track "},{"id":"spn-89162","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-89163","text":" 2026-07-25 "},{"id":"spn-89164","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status of the line:"},{"id":"spn-89165","text":" NOT frozen, per your ruling. Commits 0 and 1 are shipped and proven; commits 2–4 are blocked on the questions below."}]},{"id":"blk-47165","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89166","text":"0. Why this packet exists"}]},{"id":"blk-47166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89167","text":"Your L-0 ruling authorized Slice B in five commits and reserved two decisions for a later packet:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89168","text":"The exact "},{"id":"spn-89169","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-89170","text":" spelling and canonical route-key schema remain decisions for the Slice B ruling packet."}]}],"id":"blk-47167","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-47169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89171","text":"I built commits 0 and 1, then went looking for what commit 2 ("},{"id":"spn-89172","marks":["code"],"text":"AsyncRouteDecl"},{"id":"spn-89173","text":") actually has to produce. "},{"id":"spn-89174","marks":["bold"],"text":"The spelling turns out to be the easy half."},{"id":"spn-89175","text":" The route-key schema is not a notation question at all — it is a question about which identity substrate a world-emitted message lives in, and the Slice A substrate imposes three hard limits that the Slice A staging note does not mention."}]},{"id":"blk-47170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89176","text":"Everything in §3 is executed evidence, reproducible from the attached tree. I am not asking you to take any of it on description."}]},{"id":"blk-47171","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89177","text":"1. What shipped since the L-0 ruling"}]},{"id":"blk-47172","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89178","text":"Commit 0 — three-way CanvasGraphV1 importer "},{"id":"spn-89179","marks":["italic"],"text":"(done, proven)"}]},{"id":"blk-47173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89180","marks":["code"],"text":"import_canvas_graph_v1(canvas) -> LegacyCanvasImportV1(world, scenario, presentation)"},{"id":"spn-89181","text":". Battery "},{"id":"spn-89182","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run45"},{"id":"spn-89183","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89184","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-89185","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47174","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89186","text":"Commit 1 — Mailbox WRL Core surface declaration "},{"id":"spn-89187","marks":["italic"],"text":"(done, proven)"}]},{"id":"blk-47175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89188","text":"Exactly the form you ruled:"}]},{"id":"blk-47176","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[mailbox:mb](w=8, cap=4){}"},{"id":"blk-47177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89189","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-89190","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89191","marks":["code"],"text":"cap"},{"id":"spn-89192","text":" required; "},{"id":"spn-89193","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"},{"id":"spn-89194","text":" explicitly denotes empty structural ports; enters world identity through the existing canonical "},{"id":"spn-89195","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-89196","text":"; cannot participate in "},{"id":"spn-89197","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-89198","text":" topology. Battery "},{"id":"spn-89199","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46"},{"id":"spn-89200","text":", rows N1–N12, "},{"id":"spn-89201","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-89202","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-89203","marks":["bold"],"text":"14/14 green"},{"id":"spn-89204","text":", frozen L-0 tier untouched."}]},{"id":"blk-47178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89205","text":"Three points worth your attention:"}]},{"id":"blk-47179","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89206","marks":["bold"],"text":"The required-`{}` rule is computed, not named."},{"id":"spn-89207","text":" The parser requires a"}]}],"id":"blk-47180","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-47182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89208","text":"written port block exactly when "},{"id":"spn-89209","marks":["code"],"text":"port_projection(role)"},{"id":"spn-89210","text":" is empty, so the rule already covers the next portless role with no edit. Naming "},{"id":"spn-89211","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-89212","text":" there would have made the parser the fork §18 exists to prevent."}]},{"id":"blk-47183","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89213","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pre-freeze obligation 5.2 is discharged."},{"id":"spn-89214","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89215","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_PORT_SIGNATURE"},{"id":"spn-89216","text":" now"}]}],"id":"blk-47184","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-47186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89217","text":"carries a validator-owned "},{"id":"spn-89218","marks":["code"],"text":"ObjectKey"},{"id":"spn-89219","text":" locator and "},{"id":"spn-89220","marks":["code"],"text":"field_path"},{"id":"spn-89221","text":", verified end-to-end through "},{"id":"spn-89222","marks":["code"],"text":"diagnose_core"},{"id":"spn-89223","text":" (row N8e). It was previously the one identity-spine rejection arriving with "},{"id":"spn-89224","marks":["code"],"text":"primary_locator=None"},{"id":"spn-89225","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47187","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89226","marks":["bold"],"text":"Two more forked-vocabulary instances found and fixed"},{"id":"spn-89227","text":" (the sixth and"}]}],"id":"blk-47188","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-47190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89228","text":"seventh of the round). "},{"id":"spn-89229","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format._ROLE_LOWER"},{"id":"spn-89230","text":" was a hand-written mirror of "},{"id":"spn-89231","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir._ROLE_TOKEN"},{"id":"spn-89232","text":"; it is now the inverted table plus an injectivity assertion. Had it shipped, adding "},{"id":"spn-89233","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-89234","text":" would have produced a "},{"id":"spn-89235","marks":["code"],"text":"KeyError"},{"id":"spn-89236","text":" from inside the formatter on a world that parses, seals and runs correctly. Separately, the bootstrap surface reported "},{"id":"spn-89237","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-89238","text":" as "},{"id":"spn-89239","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"outside Forge Semantic IR v1\""},{"id":"spn-89240","text":" — true when written, false since the v1.1 registry admitted "},{"id":"spn-89241","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-89242","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89243","marks":["bold"],"text":"§18's self-emptying property held empirically."},{"id":"spn-89244","text":" Adding one dict entry made "},{"id":"spn-89245","marks":["code"],"text":"unwritable_role_ids()"},{"id":"spn-89246","text":" compute to "},{"id":"spn-89247","marks":["code"],"text":"()"},{"id":"spn-89248","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-89249","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_complete"},{"id":"spn-89250","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89251","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_spans"},{"id":"spn-89252","text":" followed with "},{"id":"spn-89253","marks":["bold"],"text":"zero edits"},{"id":"spn-89254","text":", and the L-0 sweep stayed green with "},{"id":"spn-89255","marks":["bold"],"text":"zero battery edits"},{"id":"spn-89256","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47192","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89257","text":"Mutation testing"}]},{"id":"blk-47193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89258","text":"Eleven mutants, each reverting one production edit; all eleven caught, and the harness carries a null-mutant control. That control earned its place: the harness's "},{"id":"spn-89259","marks":["bold"],"text":"first run reported 11/11 caught and every one was an artifact"},{"id":"spn-89260","text":" — the copied tree could not import "},{"id":"spn-89261","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-89262","text":" from a sibling directory it did not have, so all eleven \"detections\" were the battery failing to start."}]},{"id":"blk-47194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89263","text":"Mutation also found two defects in the battery itself:"}]},{"id":"blk-47195","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89264","marks":["bold"],"text":"N2b claimed a proof it does not deliver."},{"id":"spn-89265","text":" It asserted that "},{"id":"spn-89266","marks":["code"],"text":"(w=8,cap=4)"}]}],"id":"blk-47196","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-47198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89267","text":"and "},{"id":"spn-89268","marks":["code"],"text":"(w=4,cap=8)"},{"id":"spn-89269","text":" differ, and the comment claimed this showed the two fields are not folded into one. Under an exact fold ("},{"id":"spn-89270","marks":["code"],"text":"cap := w"},{"id":"spn-89271","text":") the worlds become (8,8) and (4,4) — still distinct, so the row sails through the very defect it advertised. Restated; N1b and N2 own that law."}]},{"id":"blk-47199","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89272","marks":["bold"],"text":"N2c had a dead conjunct."},{"id":"spn-89273","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89274","marks":["code"],"text":"a == b and a == ids[\"two\"] or a == b"},{"id":"spn-89275","text":" groups as"}]}],"id":"blk-47200","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-47202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89276","marks":["code"],"text":"(… and …) or (a == b)"},{"id":"spn-89277","text":", so the middle term could never change the verdict — and it was false anyway. Second such case this round after commit 0's ordering row."}]},{"id":"blk-47203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89278","text":"The battery is now fault-isolated per row, because mutation showed a raise inside N4d's setup aborted the section and reported the failure under "},{"id":"spn-89279","marks":["bold"],"text":"N4's"},{"id":"spn-89280","text":" name — a law that still held taking the blame for a law that had been disproved."}]},{"id":"blk-47204","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89281","text":"2. The easy half — the "},{"id":"spn-89282","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-89283","text":" spelling"}]},{"id":"blk-47205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89284","text":"The Core edge grammar is "},{"id":"spn-89285","marks":["code"],"text":"^\\[(?:\\w+:)?(\\w+)\\]\\s*--(\\w+)-->\\s*\\[(?:\\w+:)?(\\w+)\\]$"},{"id":"spn-89286","text":". A route mirrors it unambiguously; "},{"id":"spn-89287","marks":["code"],"text":"~"},{"id":"spn-89288","text":" appears nowhere else in the surface, so all candidates below lex cleanly."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-47207","spans":[{"id":"spn-89289","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-47208","spans":[{"id":"spn-89290","text":"Form"}]},{"id":"blk-47209","spans":[{"id":"spn-89291","text":"Note"}]}],"id":"blk-47206","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-47210","spans":[{"id":"spn-89292","marks":["bold"],"text":"S1"}]},{"id":"blk-47211","spans":[{"id":"spn-89293","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb]"}]},{"id":"blk-47212","spans":[{"id":"spn-89294","text":"tagged, mirrors "},{"id":"spn-89295","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-89296","text":" exactly"}]}],[{"id":"blk-47213","spans":[{"id":"spn-89297","marks":["bold"],"text":"S2"}]},{"id":"blk-47214","spans":[{"id":"spn-89298","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~> [mb]"}]},{"id":"blk-47215","spans":[{"id":"spn-89299","text":"untagged; asserts there is only ever one async relation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-47216","spans":[{"id":"spn-89300","marks":["bold"],"text":"S3"}]},{"id":"blk-47217","spans":[{"id":"spn-89301","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb] (body=0.0.0.7, every 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-47218","spans":[{"id":"spn-89302","text":"tagged + emission parameters"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-47219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89303","marks":["bold"],"text":"My recommendation: S3."},{"id":"spn-89304","text":" S1's tag slot costs nothing and keeps a second async relation available without a grammar change, matching how "},{"id":"spn-89305","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-89306","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-89307","marks":["code"],"text":"--socket-->"},{"id":"spn-89308","text":" already work. The parenthesised group is where the emitter's parameters have to go regardless of §3's outcome, and it reuses "},{"id":"spn-89309","marks":["code"],"text":"_paren_kv"},{"id":"spn-89310","text":" verbatim. S2 forecloses a relation kind to save four characters."}]},{"id":"blk-47220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89311","marks":["bold"],"text":"This is the half I am confident about, and it is not what is blocking."}]},{"id":"blk-47221","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89312","text":"3. The hard half — the route's identity substrate"}]},{"id":"blk-47222","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89313","text":"The Slice A spec stages Slice B as:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89314","text":"A minimal deterministic emitter (clock-driven, static target and payload, in the spirit of "},{"id":"spn-89315","marks":["code"],"text":"PulserDecl"},{"id":"spn-89316","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-89317","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"never data-dependent\""},{"id":"spn-89318","text":" invariant) emits during REACT into "},{"id":"spn-89319","marks":["code"],"text":"next_inbox"},{"id":"spn-89320","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-47223","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-47225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89321","text":"A delivered message borrows ADMIT identity wholesale ("},{"id":"spn-89322","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.py::_message"},{"id":"spn-89323","text":": "},{"id":"spn-89324","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"Slice A borrows ADMIT identity wholesale (§1) rather than inventing a message id\""},{"id":"spn-89325","text":"). Its identity is the "},{"id":"spn-89326","marks":["bold"],"text":"ClaimFactKey"},{"id":"spn-89327","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89328","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence, digest, payload_key)"},{"id":"spn-89329","text":", and admission keys on the "},{"id":"spn-89330","marks":["bold"],"text":"event key"},{"id":"spn-89331","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89332","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence)"},{"id":"spn-89333","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47226","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89334","text":"So a world-emitted route must produce an event key. Three limits follow, and they are the reason this is a ruling and not a commit."}]},{"id":"blk-47227","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89335","text":"F1 — A static route delivers exactly ONCE, ever"}]},{"id":"blk-47228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89336","text":"ADMIT is idempotent on event keys; that is the point of monotone claim facts. A route with a fixed "},{"id":"spn-89337","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence)"},{"id":"spn-89338","text":" and a static body re-asserts an already-accepted fact every epoch:"}]},{"id":"blk-47229","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"epoch 0  next_inbox=[(0,0,0,7)]  inbox=[]\nepoch 1  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[(0,0,0,7)]\nepoch 2  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[]\nepoch 3  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[]"},{"id":"blk-47230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89339","text":"\"Static target and payload\" therefore cannot mean a static "},{"id":"spn-89340","marks":["italic"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-89341","text":". Something in the key must advance per emission, and the only field available is "},{"id":"spn-89342","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-89343","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47231","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89344","text":"F2 — "},{"id":"spn-89345","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-89346","text":" is 4 bits"}]},{"id":"blk-47232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89347","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.py::WK = 4"},{"id":"spn-89348","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-89349","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-89350","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89351","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-89352","text":" each range 0..15, and "},{"id":"spn-89353","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario"},{"id":"spn-89354","text":" validates authored claims against exactly that range. A route emitting once per epoch therefore has at most 16 distinct keys before it wraps and starts re-asserting its own earlier facts."}]},{"id":"blk-47233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89355","marks":["code"],"text":"WK"},{"id":"spn-89356","text":" is not a free parameter: "},{"id":"spn-89357","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_ic.py"},{"id":"spn-89358","text":" derives "},{"id":"spn-89359","marks":["code"],"text":"FKEY_W = 2*WK + CKEY_W = 52"},{"id":"spn-89360","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89361","marks":["code"],"text":"EKEY_W = 2*WK"},{"id":"spn-89362","text":", so widening it changes every backend term — a backend identity event for every world in the corpus, mailbox-bearing or not."}]},{"id":"blk-47234","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89363","text":"F3 — The binding limit is 6, not 16 "},{"id":"spn-89364","marks":["italic"],"text":"(this is the one that matters)"}]},{"id":"blk-47235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89365","text":"The claim-fact log is bounded at "},{"id":"spn-89366","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS = 6"},{"id":"spn-89367","text":". A route needing a fresh key per emission consumes one fact per emission, so it emits "},{"id":"spn-89368","marks":["bold"],"text":"at most six times in the world's entire lifetime"},{"id":"spn-89369","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-47236","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"epoch 0  facts=1  emitted=yes     epoch 5  facts=6  emitted=yes\nepoch 1  facts=2  emitted=yes     epoch 6  facts=6  emitted=NO   fact_capacity_fault=1\nepoch 2  facts=3  emitted=yes     epoch 7  facts=6  emitted=NO   fact_capacity_fault=1"},{"id":"blk-47237","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89370","marks":["bold"],"text":"The saturation is announced, not silent"},{"id":"spn-89371","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-89372","marks":["code"],"text":"fact_capacity_fault"},{"id":"spn-89373","text":" latches to 1 at epoch 6, and I want to be fair to the substrate about that: it tells the truth. But a recurring route on the Slice A substrate has a hard lifetime budget of six messages, and the Spinner Bench's 9-epoch run is long enough to cross it."}]},{"id":"blk-47238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89374","text":"This is not a bug. "},{"id":"spn-89375","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-89376","text":" bounds a "},{"id":"spn-89377","marks":["italic"],"text":"monotone"},{"id":"spn-89378","text":" structure, and monotonicity is a frozen Slice A law — the log cannot GC without breaking it. It simply means "},{"id":"spn-89379","marks":["bold"],"text":"a recurring `~~` route and the claim-fact log are not obviously compatible"},{"id":"spn-89380","text":", and the staging note does not address it."}]},{"id":"blk-47239","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89381","text":"F4 — A scenario can silently cancel a world's route"}]},{"id":"blk-47240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89382","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-89383","text":" is one 4-bit space shared by world-emitted sends and scenario claims. Two sends sharing an event key with "},{"id":"spn-89384","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-89385","text":" bodies are "},{"id":"spn-89386","marks":["code"],"text":"equivocal_send"},{"id":"spn-89387","text":", and nothing is delivered:"}]},{"id":"blk-47241","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"distinct writers 3,4 -> both delivered   next_inbox=[(0,0,0,1),(0,0,0,2)]  recognition=u\nSAME key (3,0), different bodies         next_inbox=[]                     recognition=d\nSAME key (3,0), identical bodies         next_inbox=[(0,0,0,1)]            recognition=u"},{"id":"blk-47242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89388","text":"Scenarios are "},{"id":"spn-89389","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-89390","text":" part of world identity (D3). So under any scheme where a route's "},{"id":"spn-89391","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-89392","text":" lands in the scenario-authorable range, a scenario can suppress a world's own route emission without touching the world — precisely the scenario/world separation established in v0.4-0. Sixteen writers is a small space to collide in, and shipped scenarios already use writer_ids 1 and 2."}]},{"id":"blk-47243","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89393","text":"4. Questions"}]},{"id":"blk-47244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89394","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q1 — the `~~` spelling."},{"id":"spn-89395","text":" S1, S2 or S3 (§2)? "},{"id":"spn-89396","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend S3."}]},{"id":"blk-47245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89397","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q2 — the canonical route-key schema."},{"id":"spn-89398","text":" What identifies a route for canonical ordering, "},{"id":"spn-89399","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticDiff"},{"id":"spn-89400","text":", duplicate detection and diagnostic locators? (a) "},{"id":"spn-89401","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, mailbox)"},{"id":"spn-89402","text":"; (b) "},{"id":"spn-89403","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, tag, mailbox)"},{"id":"spn-89404","text":"; (c) "},{"id":"spn-89405","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, tag, mailbox, body)"},{"id":"spn-89406","text":"; (d) an authored route name. Edges are keyed structurally today, and a route needs a stable locator — "},{"id":"spn-89407","marks":["code"],"text":"ObjectKey"},{"id":"spn-89408","text":" names one object and a route names two. "},{"id":"spn-89409","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend (b), with a duplicate route a typed rejection, and a new `RouteKey` locator rather than overloading `ObjectKey`."}]},{"id":"blk-47246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89410","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q3 — the emission budget (F1–F3). This is the blocking one."},{"id":"spn-89411","text":" Options:"}]},{"id":"blk-47247","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89412","marks":["bold"],"text":"Bounded-by-declaration."},{"id":"spn-89413","text":" A route declares a finite emission count inside"}]}],"id":"blk-47248","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-47250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89414","text":"the frozen budget and is a typed rejection if it could exceed "},{"id":"spn-89415","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-89416","text":". Honest, needs no frozen change, and makes the budget visible in the source — but a \"route\" that fires six times is closer to a scheduled batch of sends than to a channel."}]},{"id":"blk-47251","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89417","marks":["bold"],"text":"A separate identity substrate for world-emitted sends"},{"id":"spn-89418","text":", so routes do not"}]}],"id":"blk-47252","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-47254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89419","text":"consume claim facts at all. Preserves recurrence and monotonicity, but it is exactly the \"inventing a message id\" that Slice A §1 deliberately refused."}]},{"id":"blk-47255","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89420","marks":["bold"],"text":"Raise `MAX_FACTS`."},{"id":"spn-89421","text":" Moves backend width; a corpus-wide identity event; and"}]}],"id":"blk-47256","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-47258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89422","text":"only postpones the wall."}]},{"id":"blk-47259","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-47261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89423","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recurrence is out of scope for Slice B"},{"id":"spn-89424","text":" — one route emits at most once,"}]}],"id":"blk-47260","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-47262","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89425","text":"and recurrence waits for "},{"id":"spn-89426","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.world.async.v1"},{"id":"spn-89427","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89428","marks":["italic"],"text":"I lean 1 or 4."},{"id":"spn-89429","text":" Both keep every frozen law intact and neither pretends the budget is not there. I do not think I should choose between them: option 4 is a scope decision about what "},{"id":"spn-89430","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-89431","text":" promotion means, and §14 promotion is yours."}]},{"id":"blk-47264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89432","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q4 — the writer namespace (F4)."},{"id":"spn-89433","text":" Reserve a sub-range of the 4-bit "},{"id":"spn-89434","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-89435","text":" space for world-emitted routes (narrowing "},{"id":"spn-89436","marks":["code"],"text":"ScenarioV1"},{"id":"spn-89437","text":"'s validated range, which rejects some currently-valid scenarios), or give world-emitted sends a disjoint identity domain, or accept scenario collisions as authored risk? "},{"id":"spn-89438","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend a reservation;"},{"id":"spn-89439","text":" authored risk makes world behaviour depend on a scenario that is deliberately outside world identity."}]},{"id":"blk-47265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89440","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q5 — which roles may source a route?"},{"id":"spn-89441","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89442","marks":["code"],"text":"Pulser"},{"id":"spn-89443","text":" only (clock-driven, matching the \"never data-dependent\" invariant), or any node? "},{"id":"spn-89444","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend Pulser only for Slice B"},{"id":"spn-89445","text":" — it is the only role that already carries a clock, and widening later is additive."}]},{"id":"blk-47266","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89446","text":"5. What I will do without a ruling"}]},{"id":"blk-47267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89447","text":"Nothing that touches these decisions. Specifically I will "},{"id":"spn-89448","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-89449","text":" guess the route key or the emission budget, because both are identity-bearing and both would be expensive to unwind after a battery pins them."}]},{"id":"blk-47268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89450","text":"I will not freeze the Slice B line: per your ruling the mailbox declaration and the first "},{"id":"spn-89451","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-89452","text":" route ship together, and "},{"id":"spn-89453","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46"},{"id":"spn-89454","text":"'s own verdict line says so. If you want the inert declaration reverted rather than left unfrozen in the tree, say so and I will pull it."}]},{"id":"blk-47269","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89455","text":"6. The attached tree"}]},{"id":"blk-47270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89456","text":"This packet ships a "},{"id":"spn-89457","marks":["bold"],"text":"runnable"},{"id":"spn-89458","text":" tree — the whole "},{"id":"spn-89459","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/"},{"id":"spn-89460","text":" module set, the battery corpus, and "},{"id":"spn-89461","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/"},{"id":"spn-89462","text":" — not an excerpt. The first draft shipped nine hand-picked files and told you to run the sweep, which that tree could not do. "},{"id":"spn-89463","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep.py"},{"id":"spn-89464","text":"'s own docstring names that failure, so it would have been a poor thing to hand you."}]},{"id":"blk-47271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89465","text":"Key files: "},{"id":"spn-89466","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/binding_run46.py"},{"id":"spn-89467","text":" (commit 1 battery, N1–N12) · "},{"id":"spn-89468","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/binding_run45.py"},{"id":"spn-89469","text":" (commit 0) · "},{"id":"spn-89470","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_ir.py"},{"id":"spn-89471","text":" (parser: "},{"id":"spn-89472","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROLE_TOKEN"},{"id":"spn-89473","text":", required-"},{"id":"spn-89474","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"},{"id":"spn-89475","text":" rule, Mailbox cfg, bootstrap branch) · "},{"id":"spn-89476","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_canonical.py"},{"id":"spn-89477","text":" (port table, "},{"id":"spn-89478","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_port_projection"},{"id":"spn-89479","text":" locator) · "},{"id":"spn-89480","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_format.py"},{"id":"spn-89481","text":" (inverted emitter vocabulary) · "},{"id":"spn-89482","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_plan.py"},{"id":"spn-89483","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89484","marks":["code"],"text":"_PlanView.mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-89485","text":" — declared and provably ignored) · "},{"id":"spn-89486","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/admit.py"},{"id":"spn-89487","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89488","marks":["code"],"text":"WK"},{"id":"spn-89489","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89490","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-89491","text":", the two seams, "},{"id":"spn-89492","marks":["code"],"text":"_message"},{"id":"spn-89493","text":") · "},{"id":"spn-89494","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_scenario.py"},{"id":"spn-89495","text":" (the shared writer space) · "},{"id":"spn-89496","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate46.py"},{"id":"spn-89497","text":" (mutation harness + null control) · "},{"id":"spn-89498","marks":["code"],"text":"FORGE_SEMANTIC_IR_v1_1_MAILBOX_SLICE_A_SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-89499","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89500","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-89501","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-47272","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89502","text":"Reproducing"}]},{"id":"blk-47273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89503","marks":["bold"],"text":"Run the sweep first"},{"id":"spn-89504","text":" — no "},{"id":"spn-89505","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-89506","text":" binary ships (it is platform-specific), and the sweep builds it from "},{"id":"spn-89507","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/c/ic32.c"},{"id":"spn-89508","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-89509","marks":["code"],"text":"gcc -O2"},{"id":"spn-89510","text":". Verified from a clean extraction on Python 3.14.2:"}]},{"id":"blk-47274","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"cd forge && python3 run_l0_sweep.py     # builds ic32; ALL PASS -- 14/14 green (135s)\ncd forge && python3 binding_run46.py    # PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE, N1-N12\ncd ..    && python3 mutate46.py         # 12 mutants, null control first: ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"blk-47275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89511","text":"With no compiler available, "},{"id":"spn-89512","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1"},{"id":"spn-89513","text":" gives "},{"id":"spn-89514","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_ONLY"},{"id":"spn-89515","text":" — every law still runs; native adds a second independent reducer, not new laws. Running "},{"id":"spn-89516","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46.py"},{"id":"spn-89517","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89518","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-89519","text":" the sweep fails one row ("},{"id":"spn-89520","marks":["code"],"text":"N12"},{"id":"spn-89521","text":") with a located "},{"id":"spn-89522","marks":["code"],"text":"FileNotFoundError"},{"id":"spn-89523","text":" for the unbuilt binary rather than a stack trace, which is the per-row fault isolation described in §1 doing its job."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraqtwa76lfa2k637bfirb26d6jaxanfzvcj227phorrm5w6i7lk33a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}